#### 8. Exception Handling *(Smell 8 — testsmells.org)*

**Test:** `ProcessOrder_EmptyOrder_ThrowsValidationError` (line 110)
**Risk:** Manual try/catch is verbose and fragile — if the exception type changes, the test silently passes via `Assert.Fail` never being reached.

```csharp
// ❌ Current — manual try/catch
try
{
    processor.ProcessOrder(order);
    Assert.Fail("Expected an exception but none was thrown");
}
catch (ValidationException ex)
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Order must contain at least one item", ex.Message);
}
```

**Fix:** Use MSTest's built-in exception assertion:

```csharp
var ex = Assert.ThrowsException<ValidationException>(
    () => processor.ProcessOrder(order));
Assert.AreEqual("Order must contain at least one item", ex.Message);
```

